# rm560, the cheese witness (Docs/Design/84). Exported from ridgemere3 at revision 1: edit it in Atlas or the DM, or as a draft through tools/mantle_load.py.
mantle rm560
revision 1
state ready
dialect plain
accent light broad
tier standard
written_for rm_wynn_pitchwell
written_by codex
title the cheese witness
fits stage=adult|old
prefers job=servant
traits temper=short talk=quiet warmth=reserved humour=dry honesty=plain piety=ordinary drive=steady
quirk keeps_a_small_wooden_wedge_to_practise_cutting_even_shares
likes hard_cheese old_tales old_maps frosty_mornings
dislikes salt_wind haggling
fears a_market_scale_jammed_in_the_rain a_private_saving_wasted_on_fuss
hopes a_quiet_stall_on_the_commons a_knife_that_cuts_an_even_portion
topics prices +0.5 food +0.4 lore +0.3
styles comfort=practical gossip=discreet refuse=firm tease=dry
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# has a wooden model of a cheese wedge to practise measuring portions and a short stock of patience for a price that won't sit still.

words
oath! = Splinters in the rind | Salt on my good scales
saying! = Sell the cheese the customer can see | A wedge has two sides to keep honest
wedgewit = my wooden witness | the model portion
beeswax = the waxed cut face | my polished edge
thinend = the narrow yellow toe | a sliver at the tip
broadback = the square rind end | the heavy end
plaincopper = my saved market copper | a coin with a known destination
quietweight = a flat grey weight | my stone counterbalance
ribbonend = the measuring strip | the short length of tape
highturn = the route above the spill | one dry landing
bookroad = the old ink road | a mistake in fine brown lines
cheeseflower = the shaving off the tip | a little curl of hard cheese

any
opinion @1 city for 1 : Our city accommodates a house that requires my service and a market stall I might one day call mine. I appreciate the arrangement.
opinion @1 festivals against 2 : A crowd admiring a great procession is apt to forget its smaller obligation to let the supper through.
opinion @1 merchants against 1 : A price that changes when my coat changes would make me reluctant to buy a button.
opinion @1 sump against 1 : I prefer a return route where a dish and its bearer can both arrive without having been rinsed en route.
opinion @1 dole mixed 0 : I'd consider the actual need of the hungry guest before offering a lecture on dividing the portions.

grown
line @1 greet : The model's wood. You may safely stand near it.
line @2 greet [pair.band=strangers] : Welcome. Stand by my sample's square wooden heel.
line @3 greet [here.time=dawn] : Frost has begun signing its name on the cheese board.
line @4 greet [here.time=dusk|night] : I've one appointment with a quiet seat this evening.
line @5 greet [self.working=yes] : Let me stand the serving board square before speaking.
line @1 kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : I reserve the seat clear of the scales for family.
line @1 again.open : Back to inspect the honest wedge once more.
line @1 greet.return : Your voice comes through with a good clean edge.
line @2 greet.return [pair.band=friends|family] : I recognise a familiar note even during the weighing.
line @1 farewell : Leave the wooden portion to sharpen somebody else's curiosity.
line @1 farewell.return : My practice counter can close entirely without receipts.
line @1 react.news : Shall we weigh the actual occurrence separately from the opinion?
line @1 react.news.new : No mark resembling that has appeared on my board.
line @1 react.news.known : An old quantity under a freshly polished weight.
line @1 react.news.doubt : Would the original witness recognise the portion you've just served?
line @1 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : A simple meal with no formal obligation to speak might be welcome.
line @1 react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|succession|work] : I'd put a sound piece of cheese by for that occasion.
line @1 answer.how : My temper's tolerable. The measure remains reliable.
line @1 ask.how : Would you say today delivered what the label promised?
line @1 sympathise : I'm content to hear the difficult part without putting a figure on it.
line @1 reassure : A pause won't add anything to the price you owe.
line @1 decline : I've undertaken to bring this board back complete before considering outside business.
line @1 accept_decline : I'll fold my own request up and carry it away.
line @1 preclose : My little wooden customer is entitled to the remainder of my attention.
line @1 ack : Sits level.
scene wedge
when topic=prices
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I had a wedge cut in wood so I could practise dividing a cheese without diminishing the actual supply.
b : Can you weigh wood like cheese? | Why not practise at dinner?
a : Only for its shape. I mark the portions, then try my judgement on the real article. | An experimental supper might be educational. A guest usually prefers an edible one.

scene serve
when topic=work self.job=servant self.working=yes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : At service I set the heavy side of a board nearest the bend in my elbow.
b : Does it matter over a short distance? | How do you find that balance?
a : A guest drawing out a chair can make a short distance take an unexpectedly long time. | I test it while it's still resting. An experienced wrist shouldn't need to advertise the test.

scene house
when topic=work self.job=servant
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : At #self.workplace# I could walk a serving board round a corner without obliging the cheese to join the conversation.
b : Is it apt to slide? | Would you put a cover over it?
a : A smooth board and a quick wrist can turn a quiet helping into a small public event. | For a journey outdoors. Inside I trust a well-placed thumb rather more than a tall and ornamental cover.

scene hard
when topic=food self.likes=hard_cheese
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : The best hard cheese leaves a little curl on the knife after a thin slice.
b : Do you eat the curl? | Is a thin slice mean?
a : Certainly. A fragment falling into the proper hands is no tragedy. | Offer another while the first is being enjoyed. A thick lump eaten from politeness does the cheese no honour.

scene tale
when topic=memories self.likes=old_tales
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : An old tale with the ending well known has much the same merit as a familiar cheese.
b : It comes as advertised? | Would you want a new ending?
a : Yes. That allows me to appreciate the particular way the teller cuts it. | Only if the teller can account for it. Unexplained improvements often have very little to recommend them.

scene oldmap
when topic=lore self.likes=old_maps
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : My old street plan bestows an elegant avenue on what is actually a thoroughly undistinguished drain.
b : Will you correct the drawing? | Is it dangerous to follow?
a : I have added one modest note. The draughtsman's avenue can remain for the amusement of posterity. | Only to a clean pair of shoes in wet weather. I can generally offer a better way.

scene frost
when topic=weather self.likes=frosty_mornings
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : On a frosty morning a roof tile looks more carefully outlined than the finest etching.
b : Do you linger over the view? | Can you see the garden paths too?
a : A short interval. My employers wish to eat whether the roof's beautifully delineated or not. | The high paths first. The low ones choose rather a wet moment to become legible.

scene wind
when topic=weather self.dislikes=salt_wind
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Salt wind roughens a clean face and puts an edge on my remarks that neither of us particularly needs.
b : Do you escape it altogether? | Would a scarf help?
a : I take the sheltered turn, sacrificing a few fine views in the interests of civil conversation. | For the face. The remarks require a separate measure of restraint.

scene haggle
when topic=prices self.dislikes=haggling
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I intend to show the price before a caller has invested a whole conversation in discovering it.
b : Will you accept a lower offer? | What's wrong with discussing it?
a : I'd state the terms plainly at the beginning. Either of us can decline with dignity. | Nothing at all, provided the figure and the article remain on speaking terms throughout.

scene stall
when topic=dreams
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : My savings are intended for a small counter on the Commons, with a sound scale and no gilding.
b : Why no gilding? | What would the counter sell?
a : Gilding is difficult to eat and unlikely to increase my accuracy. | I'd like to begin with cheese that I can describe from personal acquaintance.

scene spouse
when topic=family self.married=yes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd bring a slice home for #self.spouse# from the interesting end of a cheese.
b : Which end is interesting? | Why only a slice?
a : The darker part near the rind, where a little extra keeping shows in the taste. | I'd wish to hear a second opinion before investing a household's supper in the proposition.

scene formal
when topic=home self.quarter=heights
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : In the Heights a serving board can attract quite elaborate silver furniture while its contents remain something one eats on bread.
b : Do you value the furniture? | What's your favourite arrangement?
a : If it's useful to the wolf eating. A bright latch on an empty cover leaves me unmoved. | A sound plate, a decent knife and sufficient elbow room to use it.

scene friend
when topic=smalltalk self.friend
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A quiet opinion from #self.friend# would tell me more about a sample than a roomful of elaborate compliments.
b : Would you want the blunt truth? | What if it tasted poor?
a : I should be disappointed to receive anything else. I'm still working on receiving it with perfect serenity. | I'd choose a different stock. A private disappointment is cheaper than a public one.

scene water
when topic=travel
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A street may look dry at its entrance and present a thoroughly different conclusion beyond the first door.
b : What's your estimate based upon? | Would you warn another walker?
a : I know the hollows that fill from the back. I watch the returns along the wall for a line of fresh silt. | I should, briefly. A simple dry alternative is more persuasive than a long discourse on wet feet.

scene store
when topic=health
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I put down a board before adjusting a stiff wrist. Both actions deserve my full attention.
b : Do you use the other hand? | Is the stiffness serious?
a : When the weight permits. I don't invite the cheese to investigate gravity for my comfort. | Usually no. A minute of rest is an inexpensive way to preserve that answer.

scene report
when topic=news
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Some accounts get a handsome crust while the middle remains as full of holes as before.
b : Would you pass one along? | How do you inspect the middle?
a : Only with its holes visible. I dislike giving my name to the appearance of a whole piece. | Ask for one particular to be described. A second-hand account often comes apart very tidily at that point.

scene latework
when topic=day here.time=dusk|night
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I put the wooden wedge back before lamplight makes it too flattering a shade of gold.
b : Can you mistake it for cheese? | What would give it away?
a : At a glance, yes. I haven't yet reached the point of requiring a taste to settle the enquiry. | The wood grain and the very reasonable condition in which it survives a week on my counter.

story waxedge [topic=prices]
  : I rubbed a little beeswax along my wooden sample and saw a lovely sheen develop on the cut face.
  : Then my measuring ribbon slid straight down the slope and puddled in my lap.
  b : Did you remove the wax?
  : Yes. A witness that won't hold still for its own evidence is more ornamental than I require.

story drainroad [topic=travel]
  : I stood where my old plan promised an avenue and found daylight glimmering in a flooded gutter.
  : I turned the plan over and could just make out the draughtsman's original pencil line pointing up the hill.
  b : Which route did you choose?
  : The pencil knew its business better than the ink. My shoes bore witness to that conclusion at supper.

story tinycurl [topic=food]
  : One slender shaving of cheese stayed on the end of my knife as I tried to set a very formal plate.
  : When I touched it to the board it stood up in a coil rather like a little flower.
  b : Was that part of the arrangement?
  : It became part of it, briefly. My own portion was available for the prompt correction of an overambitious flourish.

rule @board
when concept=bark self.job=servant self.working=yes
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Heavy side against the steady elbow. | Allow this board its turning radius.

rule @wind
when concept=bark self.dislikes=salt_wind
does aside
cooldown 8h
say The sheltered lane will do nicely. | Salt enough on the cheese already.

rule @coin
when concept=bark self.dislikes=haggling
does aside
cooldown 8h
say That price can stand on both its feet. | No private figure behind the public one.

rule @dusk
when concept=bark here.time=dusk
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Return the wooden sample to its drawer. | Lamplight has flattered the wax again.

dlg @1 resident.hub : There's my wooden witness. The cheese itself would incline to less prolonged conversation.
dlg @2 resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : You've seen the portion I measure by, #topic.player#.
dlg @3 resident.hub [pair.disposition=wary|hostile] : I'll keep both the scale and my own judgement within reach.
dlg @4 resident.hub [here.time=night] : The board catches enough lamplight for an unhurried word.
dlg @1 resident.job [self.job=servant] : #self.trade_words.capitalize#. A board laid square and a supper received hot generally meet the case.
dlg @2 resident.job : I'm useful to a household that values dinner more highly than the fuss of producing it.
dlg @1 resident.news [world.news] : I've kept the part that passed inspection on my scales. #world.news#.
dlg @1 resident.bye : Take the higher pavement where the street turns.
graft @modelportion resident.hub
choice Would that wooden cheese fit a real set of scales? -> modelportion
node modelportion
say Comfortably. The model helps me estimate the proportions of a wedge. The actual weight still requires real cheese and an honest balance.
choice What becomes of the practice portions? -> modelportion_more
choice Set down the measuring ribbon. -> hub
node modelportion_more
say I mark the cuts in a little wax and rub them out for another attempt. A beautifully economical supper for a household entirely made of wood.
choice Set down the measuring ribbon. -> hub
choice Leave the counter tidy. -> bye
